{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry Entity Selection Stability.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry Entity Selection Stability.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"geometry entity selection stability geometry entity selection stability","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry Entity Selection Stability.md","fileName":"Geometry Entity Selection Stability.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Geometry Entity Selection Stability","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:45\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Simulation Geometry Quality]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Simulation Geometry Quality","geometrycreationandimport.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry Entity Selection Stability.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry Entity Selection Stability.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"geometry entity selection stability geometry entity selection stability","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Geometry Entity Selection Stability.md","fileName":"Geometry Entity Selection Stability.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Geometry Entity Selection Stability","heading":"Geometry Entity Selection Stability","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Geometry entity selection stability is the ability of material, physics, mesh, and boundary assignments to continue identifying the intended regions after a parametric rebuild or import. Explicit numeric entity IDs are fragile because topology changes can renumber them.\n\nRule-based box, ball, intersection, cumulative, or named selections express the geometric criterion instead of a transient identifier. Stable selection logic makes automated sweeps safer, but every rebuilt model still needs assignment checks.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Simulation Geometry Quality","geometrycreationandimport.pdf"],"prope